{
 "plan": {
  "title": "Donation Dashboard",
  "subtitle": "Monthly trends, top cities, payment modes, and repeat donor analysis",
  "panels": [
   {
    "id": "p1",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Total Donations",
    "sql": "SELECT SUM(\"Amount\") AS n FROM \"donor_transactions\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p2",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Unique Donors",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT \"Donor\") AS n FROM \"donor_transactions\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p3",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Repeat Donors",
    "sql": "SELECT COUNT(*) AS n FROM (SELECT \"Donor\" FROM \"donor_transactions\" GROUP BY 1 HAVING COUNT(*) > 1)",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p4",
    "kind": "kpi",
    "title": "Avg Donation",
    "sql": "SELECT AVG(\"Amount\") AS n FROM \"donor_transactions\"",
    "unit": ""
   },
   {
    "id": "p5",
    "kind": "line",
    "title": "Monthly Donation Trend",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Date\" AS month, SUM(\"Amount\") AS total FROM \"donor_transactions\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
    "x": "month",
    "y": [
     "total"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p6",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Top 10 Cities by Donations",
    "sql": "SELECT \"City\" AS city, SUM(\"Amount\") AS total FROM \"donor_transactions\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10",
    "x": "city",
    "y": [
     "total"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p7",
    "kind": "bar",
    "title": "Donations by Payment Mode",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Mode\" AS mode, SUM(\"Amount\") AS total FROM \"donor_transactions\" GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC",
    "x": "mode",
    "y": [
     "total"
    ]
   },
   {
    "id": "p8",
    "kind": "table",
    "title": "Top 10 Repeat Donors",
    "sql": "SELECT \"Donor\", COUNT(*) AS donation_count, SUM(\"Amount\") AS total_amount FROM \"donor_transactions\" GROUP BY 1 HAVING COUNT(*) > 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10"
   }
  ],
  "narrative": "The dashboard tracks the financial health of the organization through key metrics. The total amount raised is {{p1}}, driven by {{p2}} unique contributors. Among these, {{p3}} donors have given more than once, indicating strong loyalty. The average contribution size is {{p4}}. Over time, the monthly trend in {{p5}} shows the fluctuation of funds received. Geographically, the top cities listed in {{p6}} contribute the most to the cause. Payment preferences are visualized in {{p7}}, highlighting the most popular methods. Finally, the detailed list of {{p8}} identifies the most consistent supporters."
 },
